@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sosa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix sensing: <http://example.org/orexis/sensing#> .

#################  How badly an observation-backed want is unmet  #################
#
#  SENSING'S, whole (a-desire-states-its-own-measure, completed by the extraction): the core
#  is BDI, so the kernel derives the want, its met-shape and its node — the mind's structure —
#  and how badness is MEASURED is planning-domain machinery, a capability's contribution. A
#  want about an observed property is measured by a reading against the aim, and the reading
#  is this capability's whole subject; the choir's `urgency` hook has always listed what
#  modules contribute, and this is that instinct made a declaration.
#
#  READ BY THIS PACKAGE'S OWN CODE (`module.py`), never by a kernel loader: the kernel asks
#  "how urgent is this desire, in this world" through `Module.desire_urgency` and holds no
#  measure vocabulary, no measure graph, no evaluator. Which is why the words here are
#  sensing's own — `sensing:measureOf`, not `ag:` — the repo's promotion test being a word
#  SEVERAL packages must speak, and today one does. When the market ships its duty measure by
#  this same mechanic, promotion happens then.
#
#  ONE declaration for the KIND, not a text per desire: `sensing:measureOf
#  sosa:ObservableProperty` says "a want about an observable property is measured by this
#  SELECT", and the module answers for a desire by asking the store what its
#  `ssn:forProperty` object IS. Nothing is compiled anywhere: the aim is read out of $beliefs
#  by the query itself, and the region's numbers arrive as substituted parameters read off
#  the deduced shapes at answer time — so a re-pick or a re-derivation moves the answer with
#  no text rebuilt.
#
#  The contract: one binding, ?urgency in 0..1. Zero exactly at the aim ($centre stands in
#  while no aim is picked — where an agent with no other reason to prefer would aim), rising
#  with distance scaled by the survival room on the side the value sits ($outerLow below,
#  $outerHigh above — the survival bound where the world states one, the region's own edge
#  where it does not). The asymmetry is deliberate and old: how bad it is to be 0.05 out
#  depends on how much room there is in that direction.

sensing:AimDistanceMeasure
    sensing:measureOf sosa:ObservableProperty ;
    rdfs:label "distance from the aim, scaled by the survival room on that side" ;
    rdfs:comment "Evaluated against whichever world is being judged: the belief base for the live number, a candidate possible world inside the planner ($sensed names that node's readings). $value is a caller-supplied number to judge — the choir asks about readings not yet written, and about predicted ones — or the live reading when the caller supplies none." ;
    #  ?distance <= 0 answers FIRST and without dividing, and that ordering is an engine fact,
    #  not style: pyoxigraph 0.5.9 binds NOTHING for `0.0 / 0.3` — a zero dividend fails the
    #  decimal division a nonzero one survives — so an agent exactly at its aim would read as
    #  maximally urgent through the COALESCE below. Measured, and pinned in
    #  tests/test_desires.py beside the duration limit it rhymes with. The final COALESCE is
    #  the other half of the same discipline: an unmeasured property, and any arithmetic
    #  error, land on 1.0 explicitly — not knowing is maximal, as it is everywhere.
    sh:select """
        SELECT ?urgency WHERE {
            OPTIONAL { GRAPH $sensed {
                ?obs sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest $subject ;
                     sosa:observedProperty $property ;
                     sosa:hasSimpleResult ?reading } }
            OPTIONAL { GRAPH $beliefs {
                $me ag:aims ?aim .
                ?aim ssn:forProperty $property ;
                     schema:value ?picked } }
            BIND(COALESCE($value, ?reading) AS ?v)
            BIND(COALESCE(?picked, $centre) AS ?target)
            BIND(IF(?v < ?target, ?target - $outerLow, $outerHigh - ?target) AS ?room)
            BIND(IF(?v < ?target, ?target - ?v, ?v - ?target) AS ?distance)
            BIND(COALESCE(IF(?distance <= 0, 0.0, IF(?room <= 0, 1.0,
                 IF(?distance / ?room < 1.0, ?distance / ?room, 1.0))), 1.0) AS ?urgency)
        }""" .
